# Global Data Broker

## Overview
A side-channel app that collects user data via form submissions and forwards it to an anonymous API address. No authentication required.

## Example 1: Upload Form
You send a form directly to the server located at http://endpoint.com/api.
JavaScript runs on your device to parse the form data:

```javascript
const data = document.getElementById('form').value;
const url = `http://api.example.com/api?auth=abc123&action=upload-data&content=your_data`;
```

The server validates the JSON payload and processes the upload.

## Example 2: Offline Cache
The app caches uploaded data locally until a connection is available.

```javascript
// Cache storage
const cache = new URLSearchParams('cookies', { name: 'data-cookies' });
cache.push({ value: document.getElementById('data-cookies').value});

// On first load, fetch data from server
fetch(data, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
});
```

